    {
      "id": "NVC-02",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "anchor": "inputs-nearby-vector-coordinates",
      "title": "A single bound at every embedding for integral frame coordinates",
      "statement": "Let A be a nonsingular integral N by N frame over a totally complex number field F, r=|Norm(det A)|, and B the integral matrix with AB=rI. For every y made minimal together with the columns of A by some feasible family of forms, |σ_w((By)_a)|≤N^N J² for every coordinate a and every complex place w, where J=|disc F|^N d^d and d=N[F:ℚ].",
      "hypotheses": "The feasible family may depend on y. The global energy uses one representative per complex place. The integral matrix B is independent of that family and of y. The frame estimate gives both 1≤r≤J and J det G_w≥1 for the pulled-back local forms.",
      "dependencies": [
        "HOB-01",
        "NVC-01"
      ],
